  "decision": {
    "answer": "NEI",
    "explanation": "The provided evidence (pmid-23766237:f01) reports on the prevalence of TERT promoter mutations in various thyroid cancers, including papillary, follicular, poorly differentiated, and anaplastic thyroid cancers, as well as thyroid cancer cell lines. However, the evidence does not mention thyroid angiosarcoma. Therefore, there is insufficient evidence to determine the stance of TERT promoter mutations in thyroid angiosarcoma.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "document_id": "pmid-23766237",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 580,
        "quote": "We found the C228T mutation in 0 of 85 (0.0%) benign thyroid tumors, 30 of 257 (11.7%) papillary thyroid cancers (PTC), 9 of 79 (11.4%) follicular thyroid cancers (FTC), 3 of 8 (37.5%) poorly differentiated thyroid cancers (PDTC), 23 of 54 (42.6%) anaplastic thyroid cancers (ATC), and 8 of 12 (66.7%) thyroid cancer cell lines. . . . As shown in Table 3, TERT promoter mutations were significantly more prevalent in the TCPTC samples than in the CPTC and FVPTC samples, 30.8% (4/13) in the former vs 10.3% (25/243) in the latter two (P=0.046, per two-tailed Fisher's exact test)."
      }
    ],
    "unresolved": [
      "Evidence for TERT promoter mutations in thyroid angiosarcoma is missing."
    ],
